{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the clear leader at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool is the best RNA setup found so far, and that RNA dominates image (0.59 vs 0.21). The one major untested design axis within this best setup is the RNA encoder: all four completed experiments used pca_n2000. Question: Does a learned, biologically-informed encoder (scvi_n200) improve over PCA in the same multiprofile+avgpool setting? This is a clean single-variable swap relative to config_002, isolating the encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It directly tests whether the representation layer can push performance above 0.591, which is the most consequential unknown before committing budget to multimodal or other encoder variants. (2) If scvi_n200 (only 200 dims) matches or beats PCA_n2000, that strongly signals learned encoders are worth pursuing; if it falls well short, PCA is likely sufficient and budget is better spent elsewhere. (3) It avoids the confound of simultaneously changing profile setting, aggregation, or modality, making the result interpretable. (4) It is more informative than testing multimodal now, given the very weak image signal (0.21), which makes the expected multimodal gain small and the encoder question more decisive for the overall strategy."
}

